<div id="2026-09-04-traveler-location-null" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-09-04 — Traveler put_part_in_pick_box location_id NULL insert</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>ROOT CAUSE.</strong> In put_part_in_pick_box (called from Inventory/api/stock/receive_qty for item=84), code reached INSERT into inventory_stock_levels with location_id=NULL. The InventoryLocation lookup by sitename (from _sitename via stash/session or domain) returned no row for the 3d site on first pick-box receive from external script (Python urllib to :4003). Pre-fix code did not guarantee $loc_id before the stock create at (old) ~660; DB result class enforces NOT NULL on location_id + unique(item_id, location_id).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>DO.</strong> (fix already applied in tree): Ensure location resolution before any stock create. Current implementation: search active-by-sitename, fallback any-by-sitename, auto-create "Print Farm Pick Box" if needed; $loc_id = $loc->id; then stock create or reuse with location_id; defensive in txn too. Use only app paths (no raw SQL/DDL).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>DO NOT.</strong> Hand-edit DB; bypass the location guarantee; close without evidence.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>ACCEPT.</strong> Root cause matches exact log (ParamValues location_id=undef on the INSERT statement). Verified: perl -c Traveler.pm and Inventory.pm OK; code review of 589-698 confirms $loc_id always defined before use in create({location_id => $loc_id}). Existing stock fallback reuses rows safely. Changelog entry present. (Site 3d worktree, error 2026-09-03.)</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Util/Manufacturing/Traveler.pm:629-668</code> (location guarantee + stock create), <code>Comserv/lib/Comserv/Controller/Inventory.pm:2145</code> (API entry), <code>Comserv/root/Documentation/changelog/entries/2026-09-04-traveler-location-null.inc</code>.</p>
</div>